 "versioning": [
  "every message carries ver_major.ver_minor; a minor version may only append fields, use spare bits or add enumeration values and message types",
  "a receiver decodes the fields it knows and skips the rest (the packet length says how much); an unknown message type is counted and dropped",
  "an unknown enumeration value is read as the most cautious known value (enums.*.unknown_as)",
  "a major version mismatch is refused",
  "a field marked since N is absent from packets of minor version < N (a field that replaced spare bits reads as spare there), so a v0.1 packet decodes exactly as v0.1 defined it"
 ],
